    "strength": "medium",
    "remedy": "Same as the notice claim: dilution void. Section 6.3 requires 'a bona fide Company purpose set forth in the call notice,' and the library states a call lacking the stated bona fide purpose does not trigger dilution. Currently no evidence in the file that the Company needed $1.5M or had a project (QUESTIONS.md Q6); this claim needs discovery or a books-and-records production to firm up."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Bad-faith/arbitrary exercise of the Manager's Section 6.3 'good faith' fair-value discretion: the 6.1% recomputation implies a pre-money value of $630,504-$768,908, 91%-94% below the Manager's own contemporaneous $7.2M 'fair value' and the broker's $9.8M",
