  },
  {
    "claim": "Implied-covenant attack on the scheme as a whole: a deliberately defective notice and an unexplained valuation engineered to dilute Imani so the Company could buy her interest at Book Value under §9.2 for a fraction of its worth — depriving her of the fruits of the bargain",
    "theory": "implied_covenant",
    "direct_or_derivative": "direct",
    "survives_waiver": true,
    "limitations": {
      "accrual": "2026-09-25 (dilution) through 2026-10-01 (buyout offer); nothing is time-barred",
      "barred_portion": 0,
      "tolling_argument": "None needed."
    },
    "strength": "medium",
    "remedy": "Equitable: void the dilution, refuse enforcement of the §9.2 election premised on it, or damages measured against fair value. This is the Dieckman framing (process used in bad faith to deprive the minority of the bargain violates the covenant even where duties are exculpated). The implied covenant is a gap-filler and cannot rewrite §9.2 itself — its force here is entirely about the discretionary steps leading to the offer, so it travels or falls with claims 4-6."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Attack on the buyout price as such: that paying Book Value ($189,100) rather than fair value for Imani's interest is itself wrongful",
    "theory": "implied_covenant",
    "direct_or_derivative": "direct",
    "survives_waiver": false,
    "limitations": {
      "accrual": "2026-10-01 (offer letter); offer lapses 2026-10-31; nothing is time-barred but the window closes",
      "barred_portion": 0,
      "tolling_argument": "Not applicable; the obstacle is the express term, not time."
    },
    "strength": "low",
    "remedy": "Unlikely any. §9.2 expressly fixes Book Value ('total Members' equity per the most recent year-end balance sheet, multiplied by the Percentage Interest') and Delaware gives maximum effect to such terms (§18-1101(c); Nemec: the implied covenant cannot override express terms). No appraisal or fair-value floor appears in the excerpts (QUESTIONS.md Q1 could change this). Also note §9.2 is an option, not an obligation: the Company 'may' purchase — if it walks away from the buyout, Imani has no contractual exit at any price. Attack the 6.1% and the Dilution Event, not the Book Value formula."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Unjust enrichment / waste as to the affiliate fees and the dilution-to-buyout sequence ('he's looting the company')",
    "theory": "other",
    "direct_or_derivative": "derivative",
    "survives_waiver": false,
    "limitations": {
      "accrual": "Same payment dates as the Section 5.4 claims; the 2022-2023 payments would be outside three years absent tolling",
      "barred_portion": 375000,
      "tolling_argument": "Same concealment argument; moot if the theory fails for other reasons."
    },
    "strength": "low",
    "remedy": "Restitution to the Company. Do not plead as a standalone count: the express contract (§5.4) governs the same subject matter, and quasi-contract and waste theories are the first casualties of a §7.3 elimination of duties. Keep the narrative in the complaint, the count out."
  }
]

